            <ArticleTitle>Reversible severe lower limb pain during a dipyridamole sestamibi myocardial perfusion study: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>350-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 68-year-old woman reported acute severe pain in both lower limbs during a dipyridamole sestamibi myocardial perfusion scan. The pain was rapidly relieved by the administration of intravenous aminophylline. A review of the literature on the adverse effects of dipyridamole did not include this symptom.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
